    {
      "description": "Overview of the Checkout Service observability dashboard. This dashboard tracks traffic, errors, and latency using OpenTelemetry metrics and provides the starting point for investigating problems through traces and logs.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "id": 1,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "Checkout Service — Observability Overview\n\n\n# Checkout Service — Observability Dashboard\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis dashboard provides a high-level view of the **Checkout Service's health, reliability, and performance**.\n\nIt is the starting point for investigating application problems.\n\n---\n\n## What This Dashboard Tracks\n\n### 📈 Traffic\nHow many checkout requests are the application receiving?\n\n**Metric:** `checkout_requests_total`\n\n### ❌ Errors\nHow many checkout requests are failing?\n\n**Metric:** `checkout_errors_total`\n\n### ⏱️ Latency\nHow long are checkout requests taking?\n\n**Metric:** `checkout_request_duration`\n\nWe will use this metric to monitor **p95 API latency** and identify slow requests.\n\n---\n\n## Observability Investigation Flow\n\n**Metrics → Traces → Logs**\n\n- **Metrics** tell us **that something is wrong**.\n- **Traces** help us understand **where the request is spending time**.\n- **Logs** help us understand **why the problem occurred**.\n\n### Example\n\n**High p95 latency**\n→ Find a slow request  \n→ **Inspect the trace**  \n→ Identify the slow operation  \n→ **Use the Trace ID to find related logs**  \n→ Understand the actual failure or cause\n\n---\n\n## Telemetry Pipeline\n\n**Node.js Application**\n→ **OpenTelemetry**\n→ **OTel Collector**\n→ **Prometheus / Tempo / Loki**\n→ **Grafana**",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.2.0",
      "title": "New panel",
      "type": "text"
    },
